WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:04.003
Unit fifteen. Basic Terminal Commands!

2
00:00:04.945 --> 00:00:09.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:13.476
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.526 --> 00:00:17.870
Today we learn about Basic Terminal Commands. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:22.500
Terminal. Say it with me. Terminal!

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.433
Command line. Say it with me. Command line!

7
00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:37.858
Directory. Say it with me. Directory!

8
00:00:41.299 --> 00:00:46.099
File navigation. Say it with me. File navigation!

9
00:00:49.644 --> 00:00:53.440
Command. Say it with me. Command!

10
00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:01.973
Text interface. Say it with me. Text interface!

11
00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:09.282
Execute. Say it with me. Execute!

12
00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:17.780
Programmer tool. Say it with me. Programmer tool!

13
00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:30.807
The terminal is a command line, text interface for navigating a directory. I execute a command to move through files, a tool many programmers use.

14
00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:34.213
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:40.172
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.222 --> 00:01:41.372
Directory!

17
00:01:42.452 --> 00:01:47.999
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:49.199
Execute!

19
00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:59.675
Did you know? Before computer mice and graphical interfaces became common, typing commands in a terminal was the main way people used computers!

20
00:01:59.725 --> 00:02:02.030
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:03.293 --> 00:02:13.281
Think and answer. Why might a programmer prefer using terminal commands instead of clicking with a mouse?

22
00:02:13.331 --> 00:02:14.481
Great answer!

23
00:02:15.707 --> 00:02:21.036
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.086 --> 00:02:24.273
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

